    <briefdescription>
<para>Explicit <ref refid="classConfigurator_1a656bf84cc5f0920ae21cd952164fbaef" kindref="member">Configurator::get&lt;T&gt;()</ref> specializations that expose each configuration section. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classConfigurator" kindref="compound">Configurator</ref> class declares a generic get&lt;T&gt;() accessor but does not define its behaviour for any particular type. This file supplies one explicit specialization per configuration section. Each one simply returns the matching private member stored in the <ref refid="classConfigurator" kindref="compound">Configurator</ref> object. In plain words: this file is the lookup table that maps a type name, such as <ref refid="structServerConfig" kindref="compound">ServerConfig</ref>, to the actual settings object of that type held by the <ref refid="classConfigurator" kindref="compound">Configurator</ref>.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: Code throughout the server asks for its settings by type, for example <computeroutput>store.config().get&lt;<ref refid="classConfigurator_1aec113448232bb2cde090d19e8b2b716e" kindref="member">Configurator::ServerConfig</ref>&gt;()</computeroutput>. Those calls only link successfully because this file defines each specialization. Without it, the compiler accepts the calls but the linker reports undefined references, so the server cannot obtain any of its configuration sections at runtime. Keeping the definitions here (not in the header) also means adding a new section requires updating this single mapping.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>C++ concepts and constraints: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/constraints">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/constraints</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Explicit (full) template specialization: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/template_specialization">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/template_specialization</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Function templates: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/function_template">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/function_template</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
